# Trivy ignore list — reviewed, non-applicable advisories only.
# Mirrors the accepted-risk set in osv-scanner.toml and pnpm.auditConfig
# (package.json). Keep the rationale in sync across all three.

# react-router RSC-mode CSRF bypass. The client is a Vite SPA using
# react-router in library mode only (no RSC), so it does not apply. The fix
# (react-router 8) requires a React 18->19 migration, tracked separately.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# brace-expansion ReDoS. The tree resolves to 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.8, all at or
# above the maintainer's per-line security patches (1.1.12/2.0.2/5.0.8); OSV's
# affected-versions list for the 1.x line tops out at 1.1.11, so 1.1.16 is
# patched. The scanners over-report across major lines. CVE-2026-14257 is the
# CVE alias of GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (Trivy matches by CVE); both are listed.
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg
CVE-2026-14257

# image-size infinite-loop DoS (crafted JXL/HEIF box-types, and a zero-length
# ICNS entry). No fixed version exists — OSV lists every version through 2.0.2
# as affected, including the whole 2.x line — so there is nothing to bump to.
# Reached only via metro -> @react-native/community-cli-plugin, React Native's
# build-time bundler; the images parsed are this repo's committed assets, not
# remote input. Mirrored in osv-scanner.toml with an ignoreUntil of 2026-11-30.
# CVE aliases listed alongside the GHSAs because Trivy matches by CVE.
GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq
CVE-2025-71329
GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr
CVE-2025-71330
